#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Universal clipped script
#
# A cross-platform shell utility for copying and pasting text to/from the 
# system clipboard. Works consistently across macOS, Linux, FreeBSD, and other
# Unix-like systems by automatically detecting available clipboard utilities.
#
# Author: Ben Davis <bengineerdavis@gmail.com>
# Updated: 2025-09-02 by Ben Davis <bengineerdavis@gmail.com>
#
# Usage:
#   clipped [command]
#
# Commands:
#   copy, c     Copy from stdin to system clipboard
#   paste, p    Paste from system clipboard to stdout
#   --help, -h  Show this help message
#   --version   Show version information
#
# Examples:
#   echo 'hello world' | clipped copy
#   clipped paste
#   ls -la | clipped c
#   clipped p > output.txt
#   cat file.txt | clipped copy && clipped paste
#
# Dependencies:
#   macOS: Built-in pbcopy/pbpaste (no additional dependencies)
#   Linux: xclip, xsel, or wl-copy (Wayland)
#   FreeBSD/OpenBSD/NetBSD: xclip or xsel
#   Other Unix: pbcopy/pbpaste (if available)
#
# Notes:
#   - Automatically detects and uses available clipboard utilities
#   - Prioritizes native tools (pbcopy on macOS) over alternatives
#   - Supports both X11 and Wayland display servers on Linux
#   - Falls back to pbcopy/pbpaste if available on non-Darwin systems
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MIT License
#
# Copyright (c) 2025 Ben Davis - bengineerdavis@gmail.com
#
# Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
# of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
